^["done"]{
 # Local history: written incrementally, finalized at merge.
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-10-12 19:07] decide — Creator asked for editor improvements in syntax highlighting, refactoring, tooling integrations, memory inspection, performance checks, intermediate representation and expression geometry inspection. This plan holds the instrument set the three editors share; highlighting lives in vscode-cognitive-surface, refactoring in refactor-experiment-lifecycle and citation-navigation, server features in their owner plans.
 >>[2026-10-12 20:09] implement — Landed: VS Code 99e6d993, IntelliJ 155cfd57, Neovim 1bb4f68d; all three pair inspect memory with mem list and project through emit ir. ed606b3a made file instruments work in mounted consumers.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:59] revise — The three editors' instruments landed (99e6d993, 155cfd57, 1bb4f68d); next is the parity fixture. Scorecard bug 7 now sits in this plan's own output path: reports open as dirty untitled documents (host.ts 57 and seven other call sites); readonly_reports owns it.
 >>[2026-10-25 20:40] note — A mounted consumer asks (2026-10-25, rank 3, one_probe) for one request that takes buffer text and answers form, stack, tokens, structure, and trace. Today VS Code probes the live buffer through the LSP, Neovim passes a range through --text and otherwise reads the saved file, and IntelliJ reads the saved file; Neovim and IntelliJ still start the server with npm run lsp instead of the bundled dist/server/spw-lsp.cjs. Neovim three-step inspect is the shape the consumer wants the other two to show.
}
